-- title:
--   Local twisted zeta integral for a non-scalar σ-conjugacy class
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ of degree $2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$ with completion $K_v$, let $c \in K_v^\times$, and let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$. Assume $\delta$ satisfies [`AutomorphicForm.IsNormOf`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L217) for the scalar matrix $c$, i.e. there is $y$ conjugating the norm string of $\delta$ to the image of $c\cdot 1$, and that for no unit $z$ of $L \otimes_K K_v$ is the scalar $z \cdot 1$ of the form $x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(x)$ (no $\sigma$-conjugacy to a scalar). Let $\tau'$ be a Haar measure on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser $T' = \{t : t\delta\sigma(t)^{-1} = \delta\}$, taken with its Borel structure, and let $t_v \in [0,\infty]$ satisfy $q_v \cdot \tau'(U_0) = t_v + \tau'(U_0)$, where $q_v = \mathrm{absNorm}(v)$ and $U_0 \subseteq T'$ is the set of $t$ whose determinant is $1 \otimes s$ for a unit $s$ of $K_v$ with $|s| = 1$. Then: $t_v \neq \infty$; for every real $s' \ge 1$, the lower integral over $\{t \in T' : \det t = 1 \otimes s,\ |s| = q_v^{-n} \text{ for some } n \in \mathbb{N}\}$ of $\mathrm{ofReal}\big(\|N_{(L\otimes_K K_v)/K_v}(\det t)\|^{s'}\big)$ against $\tau'$ equals $\big(t_v (q_v-1)^{-1}(1-q_v^{1-2s'})\big)\cdot (1-q_v^{-2s'})^{-1}(1-q_v^{1-2s'})^{-1}$; the factor $t_v (q_v-1)^{-1}(1-q_v^{1-2s'})$ is finite for all $s' \ge 1$; and that factor, as a function of $s'$, tends to its value at $s'=1$ as $s' \to 1^+$.
--
--   This is the local zeta integral of the twisted orbital data at a place where the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser is anisotropic ($\delta$ not $\sigma$-conjugate to a scalar), packaging the closed form, finiteness and right-continuity at $s'=1$ of the correction factor $t_v(q_v-1)^{-1}(1-q_v^{1-2s'})$. It feeds the choice of level in the construction of the automorphic data and a companion computation of the same integral over the determinant-integral part of the twisted centraliser.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_ne_top_and_setLIntegral_iUnion_detShell_twistedCentralizer_norm_algebraNorm_det_rpow_eq_mul_and_tendsto_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two.lean

